Copy the following pipeline. You paste it into the editor in a later step:

```alloy
prometheus.exporter.unix "default" { }

prometheus.scrape "default" {
  targets    = prometheus.exporter.unix.default.targets
  forward_to = [prometheus.relabel.team.receiver]
  job_name   = "integrations/node_exporter"
}

prometheus.relabel "team" {
  forward_to = [prometheus.remote_write.grafana_cloud.receiver]

  rule {
    action       = "replace"
    target_label = "team"
    replacement  = argument.attributes.value["team"]
  }
}

prometheus.remote_write "grafana_cloud" {
  endpoint {
    url = "<PROMETHEUS_REMOTE_WRITE_URL>"

    basic_auth {
      username = "<METRICS_USERNAME>"
      password = sys.env("GCLOUD_RW_API_KEY")
    }
  }
}
```

This pipeline:

1. Collects Linux host metrics with `prometheus.exporter.unix` and scrapes them.
1. Adds a `team` label with `prometheus.relabel`. The `argument.attributes.value["team"]` expression reads the `team` attribute of the collector that runs the pipeline.
1. Sends the labeled metrics to Grafana Cloud with `prometheus.remote_write`.

Before you paste the pipeline, replace the following placeholders:

- `<PROMETHEUS_REMOTE_WRITE_URL>`: The Prometheus remote write URL of your stack.
- `<METRICS_USERNAME>`: The Prometheus username of your stack.

The `GCLOUD_RW_API_KEY` environment variable holds your access policy token, so you don't enter the token in the pipeline.
